# Migration and Porting Rules

**Port status (2026-06-26):** Theme + all plugins copied from production. DB + uploads still pending.

When helping with remaining migration work:

## Port order (remaining)

1. ~~Theme + plugins~~ (done) → 2. DB import → 3. Uploads sync → 4. URL search-replace → 5. Parity testing

## Do not port

- `twintack2025-previous` (unless extracting specific code)
- Duplicate plugin version folders (`twintack-grip-manager 1-4-2`, etc.)
- Committed WooCommerce/ACF vendor trees
- One-off debug scripts unless moved to `tools/` with local-only warnings
- `wp-config*.php`, `.env`, credentials

## After porting

- Run URL audit: search for `twintack.com` in theme/plugin source
- Verify plugin activation without fatal errors
- Update `docs/PLUGIN_INVENTORY.md`
- Suggest `wp search-replace` for DB after import (see `docs/LOCAL_SETUP.md`)

## Database and media

- Guide user to import via Local Adminer or WP-CLI — never commit SQL dumps
- Stripe: test mode locally
- Disable or redirect production webhooks (Make.com, etc.)

## Suggest branch

Port work belongs on `migration/*` branches, merged to `develop` when parity is verified.
